# redlink-pwa — editor rules

Vue 3 (`<script setup>`) + Vite PWA, plain JavaScript (no TypeScript in this repo —
don't introduce `.ts`/`tsconfig.json` or TS-only syntax; there is no `any` to ban
because there is no type system here). AWS Amplify (GraphQL) backend. Tailwind for
styling, PrimeVue for UI components, vue-i18n for copy.

## Naming

- **Composables**: `useXxx.js` in `src/composables/`, one exported function
  `export function useXxx() { ... }` returning a plain object of refs/computed/functions.
  Match the file name to the exported function name (`useAnimals.js` → `useAnimals`).
- **Components**: PascalCase filenames (`PhoneInput.vue`, `AppDatePicker.vue`,
  `DashboardSidebar.vue`). Multi-word names are not required
  (`vue/multi-word-component-names` is off in eslint.config.js) but prefer them for
  anything that isn't a page-level view.
- **Views**: PascalCase, suffixed `View.vue`, under `src/views/<area>/` where `<area>`
  mirrors the route/role (`auth/`, `dashboard/owner/`, `dashboard/clinic/`).
- **Services**: kebab-case, suffixed `-service.js`, under `src/services/` — reserved for
  pure, framework-free functions (see "Deep modules" below).
- **Functions/variables**: camelCase. Async data-fetchers read as `fetchX`/`listX`;
  mutators read as `createX`/`updateXDetails`/`deleteXById`.
- **Constants/enums**: PascalCase export names, `UPPER_SNAKE` values, grouped in
  `src/constants/enums.js`, always `Object.freeze`d.

## Component structure (`.vue` files)

Order inside `<script setup>`, matching the existing components:

1. Framework/library imports (`vue`, `vue-router`, `vue-i18n`, third-party)
2. Local imports (`@/composables/...`, `@/constants/...`, `@/services/...`)
3. `defineOptions` (only when needed, e.g. `inheritAttrs: false`)
4. `defineEmits` before `defineProps`
5. Local reactive state (`ref`/`computed`)
6. `watch`/`onMounted` and other lifecycle/effects
7. Handler functions (`handleXxx`, or the specific verb for the action)

Use `@/...` path aliases, never relative `../../..` climbs, for anything outside the
current directory.

## Enums over string literals

`src/constants/enums.js` is the single source of truth for domain values
(`Species`, `RequestStatus`, `MissionStatus`, `RequestType`, `BloodGroupsBySpecies`,
`DonationFrequency`). Import from there — never hardcode `'OPEN'`, `'EMERGENCY'`,
`'DOG'`, etc. as string literals in composables or components. If a value doesn't
have an enum entry yet, add one instead of inlining the string.

## Composables: own data + state, not navigation

A composable returns `{ data refs, isLoading/isSaving, action functions }` and nothing
else. It must not call `useRouter()` or perform `router.push(...)` itself — the calling
view owns navigation after `await`ing the composable's action. (Some existing
composables violate this — don't copy that pattern into new code.)

## GraphQL calls

- Always go through `generateClient()` from `aws-amplify/api`, with an explicit
  `authMode: 'userPool'`.
- Wrap every call in `try/catch/finally`, toggling a dedicated loading ref
  (`isLoading`/`isSaving`/`isAccepting`) in `finally`.
- Prefer the `*Simple` mutations in `src/graphql/custom-mutations.js` when a full
  relation-graph mutation would otherwise error on nested fields.
- Log failures via `console.error('<French, contextual message>:', error)` before
  rethrowing or resetting state — match the existing French error-message style used
  throughout the composables.

## Deep modules for domain logic

Pure business rules (blood/species compatibility, distance calculation, eligibility)
belong in `src/services/*-service.js` as framework-free exported functions — no Vue
reactivity, no GraphQL client, no DOM. `src/services/eligibility-service.js` is the
reference shape: small interface (`checkEligibility` as the composite seam, plus its
five underlying criteria functions), everything else internal. Route new domain rules
through the existing service file for the same domain rather than reimplementing the
rule inline in a composable or component — check
for an existing rule before writing a new one.

## i18n

User-facing copy goes through vue-i18n keys backed by `src/locales/*.json`. The
`@intlify/vue-i18n/no-missing-keys` eslint rule is `error` — a key referenced in code
that isn't in the locale JSON fails lint. Don't hardcode UI strings when a locale key
convention already exists for that screen; when hardcoding is unavoidable (rare, e.g. a
brand-new screen with no established key yet), match the existing French phrasing style
used elsewhere before wiring i18n.

## Linting

Runs `eslint . --fix --cache` (`npm run lint` / `pnpm lint`). Prettier formatting is
delegated (`skipFormatting` in eslint.config.js) — don't fight the formatter, don't hand
format.
